  "notes": "Cash-basis village (governmental funds modified cash basis; Sewer proprietary fund on accrual/net position statements). Trimmed PDF (find_pages v8, 13 pages): government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), Statement of Activities (p2-4), governmental funds Balance Sheet - modified cash basis (p5), governmental funds Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p6-8), Sewer Fund net position (p9), revenues/expenses (p10), cash flows (p11), total primary government budgetary comparison (p12-13). Governmental receipts/disbursements, transfers and balances now come from the governmental funds statement Totals column (p6-8), replacing the earlier figures derived from the all-funds budget schedule: beginning fund balance (cash) 355,723, revenues 107,732, expenditures 156,213, transfers out 43,834 (to the Sewer Fund, matching its 43,834 transfer in), ending 263,408 = cash in bank 258,976 + cash at county treasurer 4,432 (p5); roll-forward ties. Interfund transfers among governmental funds (General out 63,121 and Debt Service out 1,204 vs Street in 10,414, Recreation in 10,077) are eliminated in the statement's Adjustments column (20,491), so Totals transfers in = 0. The budget schedule's transfers 64,325 = 20,491 + 43,834, and its General Government line 121,912 = expenditures 57,587 + transfers out 63,121 + 1,204, so budget function lines include transfers (split out in detail). Small differences between statements: fund statement Pro Rate Motor Vehicle 69 / Property Tax Credit 2,896 vs Statement of Activities 73 / 2,892 (same 2,965 total); fund statement used. Business-type: Sewer fund from p10, net position measure; roll-forward 477,233 + 70,857 + 1,413,987 + 3,292 - 106,178 - 49,576 + 43,834 = 1,853,449. Proprietary field left null (basis cash). Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (p1). Detail = the all-funds budget schedule (p12-13), the only supplementary schedule: lines as printed with budget_final; it mixes governmental and sewer revenue (Federal 1,980,987 and Other Local 584,932 are mostly sewer grants/loan advances, recorded business-type with review), and its General Government line 121,912 includes transfers out 64,325, split out as other financing (57,587 expenditure, computed). Read pages 1-13 of 13 Detail (user 2026-10-27): per-fund lines from the fund statements' columns (p6-8, p10) replace the combined schedule.",
